    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d145">

                <pb facs="0263" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg193"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 349.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 15, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Sir: Since my previous despatches were put into the mail General McClellan
                    reports that the battle yesterday mentioned in his telegram proves to have been
                    a complete victory. The enemy was routed, and he fled during the night.
                    McClellan is in pursuit.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
